Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tcpm: reset the hard reset budget on every unattach

tcpm_detach() only clears hard_reset_count when CC already reads open. When
the detach is triggered by VBUS loss first (seen on a OnePlus 7 Pro unplugged
from a PC after two unanswered hard resets), the count survives, and on the
next attach SNK_WAIT_CAPABILITIES goes straight to SNK_READY: the new partner
(a USB-C dock acting as source) never gets PD, so no contract and no
DisplayPort alternate mode. Give every new attach a fresh budget by clearing
the count when entering SNK_UNATTACHED/SRC_UNATTACHED.
Nura-Category: upstream-fix
Nura-Origin: nura rc4h dock debugging
Upstream-Status: not in mainline v7.2 (resets only when CC is open)
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c	2026-11-13 21:07:03.506819991 +0100
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c	2026-11-13 21:07:20.079949867 +0100
@@ -4799,6 +4799,7 @@
 		if (!port->non_pd_role_swap)
 			tcpm_swap_complete(port, -ENOTCONN);
 		tcpm_src_detach(port);
+		port->hard_reset_count = 0;	/* see SNK_UNATTACHED */
 		if (port->potential_contaminant) {
 			tcpm_set_state(port, CHECK_CONTAMINANT, 0);
 			break;
@@ -5057,6 +5058,13 @@
 			tcpm_swap_complete(port, -ENOTCONN);
 		tcpm_pps_complete(port, -ENOTCONN);
 		tcpm_snk_detach(port);
+		/*
+		 * A new attach gets a fresh hard reset budget. tcpm_detach()
+		 * only clears it when CC already reads open, which misses a
+		 * detach triggered by VBUS loss; the next partner then never
+		 * gets PD (no Source_Caps wait, straight to SNK_READY).
+		 */
+		port->hard_reset_count = 0;
 		if (port->potential_contaminant) {
 			tcpm_set_state(port, CHECK_CONTAMINANT, 0);
 			break;
